# Template. Copy to  supabase/.env  (which is git-ignored) and edit that copy.
# The Supabase CLI auto-loads supabase/.env and substitutes these values into
# the env(...) refs in config.toml (the [auth.email.smtp] block).

# --- Outbound email (auth confirmation + password-reset links) --------------
# DEFAULT below = the local Mailpit test inbox (http://127.0.0.1:54324).
# Signups work out of the box; mail is captured, not delivered.
#
# To send REAL email (local AND, after `supabase config push`, hosted),
# switch the five values to Brevo — free, 300/day, any recipient, no domain:
#   1. Sign up free at https://www.brevo.com
#   2. Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs -> Senders -> add arcooreacc@gmail.com,
#      click the link Brevo emails you to verify it.
#   3. SMTP & API -> SMTP tab: copy the "Login", generate an SMTP key.
#   4. Set:
#        SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
#        SMTP_PORT=587
#        SMTP_USER=<the Login from step 3>
#        SMTP_PASS=<the xsmtpsib-... key from step 3>
#        SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=arcooreacc@gmail.com
#   5. ./.tools/supabase.exe stop && ./.tools/supabase.exe start

SMTP_HOST=inbucket
SMTP_PORT=1025
SMTP_USER=mailpit
SMTP_PASS=mailpit
SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=arcooreacc@gmail.com
